skill: "nps-sentiment-root-cause"
sections[3]:
  - "# nps-sentiment-root-cause\n\nCluster NPS and CSAT verbatims into themes, link them to measurable drivers, and assign remediation owners. Use after each NPS or CSAT wave closes, when detractor share moves without an obvious incident, or quarterly when the remediation backlog is reviewed.\n\nOwner: role-churn-analyst (pod-customer, customer_success). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"verbatim export with score, respondent segment and date; product incident timeline; previous sentiment-report.toon for trend comparison\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/customer/sentiment-report.toon with themes[] (share, score delta, driver link, remediation owner), detractor_drivers[], closure tracking\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Export verbatims for one wave and deduplicate repeated submissions from the same account; dedupe rules are recorded in the report.\n2. Clean the text: strip boilerplate and signatures; keep original wording for evidence, never paraphrase a quote into the theme description.\n3. Cluster verbatims into themes with run_command; a theme must hold a minimum share of the wave (policy default 5 percent) or it is noise, not a finding.\n4. Score each theme by detractor share and by the score gap between mentions and silence; both numbers go in the report so hot themes are visible even with small shares.\n5. Link each theme to a measurable driver where one exists (load time, ticket resolution days, missing capability); themes without a driver link are marked as survey-only and cannot carry actions.\n6. Cross-check the top themes against the incident timeline: a theme spiking in the incident window is attributed to the incident, not to a trend.\n7. Assign one remediation owner per actionable theme with a due metric; owners are confirmed with ask_question before publication.\n8. Write sentiment-report.toon with trend against the previous wave and track remediation closure rate; unclosed themes roll into the next wave's report.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nremediation items to named owners; trend brief to product and support leads.\n"
